<title>UK: Dow Corning sets claim deadline.</title>
<headline>Dow Corning sets claim deadline.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dow Corning Corp set a deadline of Feb 14, 1997 on Thursday for anyone outside the U.S. wanting to make a claim against the company over breast and other implants.</p>
<p>Dow Corning vice president Barie Charmichael said in a statement that &quot;anyone who thinks they may have a claim against Dow Corning must act now.&quot;</p>
<p>The company, a 50-50 joint venture of Dow Chemical Co and Corning Inc, filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection in the U.S. last year amid a barrage of legal claims from women alleging that its breast implants caused a raft of health problems.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
